+# Changelog
+
+All notable changes to tally are documented here.
+Format follows [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/).
+
+## [Unreleased]
+
+### Added
+- `budget` subcommand (`tally budget --month YYYY-MM`) — shows each configured
+  category's spending versus its monthly limit. Output includes the amount spent,
+  the budget cap, and a status of `ok`, `warn` (≥ 80 % of budget), or `over`
+  (limit exceeded). Budgets and the warn threshold are configured in
+  `tally/config.py` via `CATEGORY_BUDGETS` and `BUDGET_WARN_RATIO`.
+
+## [2.0.0] — 2026-07-06
+
+Initial public release.
+
+### Added
+- `add` subcommand — record an expense with amount, category, optional currency,
+  date, and note.
+- `report` subcommand — category totals for a month, filterable to a single
+  category.
+- `list` subcommand — individual expense rows for a month or category.
+- `export` subcommand — write all expenses to CSV (stdout or a file).
+- `stats` subcommand — overall count, total, average, and date span.
+- Multi-currency support: amounts are converted to USD at record time using the
+  fixed rate table in `tally/rates.py`; all reports are denominated in USD.
+- Single-file JSON store with schema versioning and forward migration support.
